![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

Redefine `compareNatural` to use a strict lexicographical byte-order comparison instead of `Intl.Collator` with an `undefined` locale to ensure deterministic, locale-independent sorting across all runtime environments.

```suggestion
function compareNatural(left, right) {
  const s1 = normalizedString(left);
  const s2 = normalizedString(right);
  if (s1 < s2) return -1;
  if (s1 > s2) return 1;
  return 0;
}
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. Avoid using Intl.Collator with an undefined locale for sorting, as it can introduce locale-sensitive discrepancies across different runtime environments. Instead, use a strict lexicographical byte-order comparison to ensure locale-independent, deterministic ordering.
</details>

